batchPlan:
  migrationGoal: Replace 5s REST-poll / DB-hop / level-triggered signal->execution pipeline with KiteTicker WebSocket push, in-process event-driven, edge-triggered design (write-behind audit + tick-driven exits with exchange-side SL backstop).
  sequencing: INFRA_FIRST_DEPENDENCY_ORDER (R1 feed -> R2 context -> R3 edge exec -> R4 write-behind -> R5 tick exits+SL)
  rollout: DIRECT_REPLACEMENT (old poll paths removed as each batch lands; no feature flag)
  batchSizeRule: 5-10 files per batch
  preFlight: git tag pre-migration-baseline before Batch 1; each batch tagged on green verify (Step 7)

batches[5]{id,requirement,goal,files,patterns,rollbackTag,verify}:
  B1,R1,"KiteTicker market-data feed replaces the 5s option-chain poll and feeds tier3-signal","services/kite/market-ticker.ts(new); services/kite/kite-option-chain.ts; services/market/tier3-signal.ts; services/market/scheduler.ts; src/index.ts","P1,P2,P3","batch1-websocket-feed","computeChainMetrics parity vs old getQuote path; recordObservation fed by ticks; computeIntradaySignal output unchanged for identical stream; ticker reconnect+resubscribe works"
  B2,R2,"Slow-path inputs move to an atomically-swapped in-memory HotContext; hot path stops SELECTing them","services/market/hot-context.ts(new); services/market/scheduler.ts; services/kite/signal-executor.ts; services/market/index.ts","P4","batch2-hot-context","HotContext published each ensemble cycle; deriveBaseOptionSignal reads context not DB row; no behavior change vs snapshot-read values"
  B3,R3,"Execution becomes edge-triggered via per-user position-state machine; 5s executor loop removed","services/kite/tick-evaluator.ts(new); services/kite/position-state.ts(new); services/kite/signal-executor.ts; services/kite/signal-executor-scheduler.ts; src/index.ts","P5,P6","batch3-edge-trigger","one BUY_CALL direction produces NO re-entry churn; transitions fire once with cooldown; state machine covers FLAT->PENDING_ENTRY->OPEN->PENDING_EXIT->FLAT"
  B4,R4,"Postgres demoted to async write-behind audit; material-change gate dropped from signal path","lib/audit-queue.ts(new); services/market/scheduler.ts; services/kite/signal-executor.ts; services/kite/position-monitor.ts","P7,P8","batch4-write-behind","tick->order chain never awaits a DB write; snapshots/signals/executions still persisted; Resolution scheduler + trading UI still read data; gate only in audit throttle"
  B5,R5,"Position monitor goes tick-driven; exchange-side SL-M backstop placed on entry","services/kite/position-monitor.ts; services/kite/orders.ts; services/kite/position-monitor-scheduler.ts; services/kite/market-ticker.ts; src/index.ts","P9,P10","batch5-tick-exits-sl","ratchet evaluated per tick on held instruments; SL-M placed on entry at hard-stop, replaced as ratchet rises, cancelled on exit; no double-exit; exit retry ladder + 0.05 tick rounding preserved"

crossBatchNotes[4]:
  - scheduler.ts touched in B1/B2/B4; signal-executor.ts in B2/B3/B4 -> incremental edits, re-verify prior patterns each time
  - market-ticker.ts created in B1, extended in B5 to also track held-instrument tokens for exits
  - index.ts touched in B1/B3/B5 -> final wiring: start ticker+evaluator, stop removed 5s loops, keep ensemble + token-refresh schedulers
  - websocket.ts existing per-user ticker: decide in B1 whether market-ticker.ts absorbs it or coexists (order_update postback path must survive either way)

riskGuards[5]:
  - LIVE MONEY: do not deploy a half-migrated batch across market open; each batch must be green before the next
  - B3 is the churn-fix batch and the highest-behavior-change; extra scrutiny on cooldown + state transitions
  - B5 double-exit risk: SL-M backstop + in-process limit exit must be mutually exclusive (cancel SL-M before/at limit exit)
  - Reconnect storms (B1): backoff + single global ticker to avoid Kite rate limits / duplicate subscriptions
  - Parity checks in B1/B2 compare new path output to old path before old path is deleted

rollbackProcedure: On failed verify, git reset --hard <previous batch tag>; fix forward in a fresh attempt; never leave main in a half-migrated hot-path state.

testStrategy:
  framework: TypeScript project -> Vitest/Jest per repo config (confirm at Step 6); existing test seen: services/kite/__tests__/execute-hit.test.ts
  perBatch: unit-test new pure fns (computeChainMetrics, computeRatchetStop, position-state transitions, audit-queue drain); integration-test the edge-trigger no-churn invariant
